  "equipment_type": "Sensor (humidity and temperature probe)",
  "applies_to": "HMP60/HMP110-series probes ordered with the Modbus RTU option (user guide M211060EN-N).",
  "summary": "The HMP60 and HMP110 families are small Vaisala HUMICAP humidity and temperature probes. Units ordered with the Modbus option speak Modbus RTU on RS-485. This map covers the humidity and temperature readings and calculated parameters, error and status registers, filtering, serial settings and the test registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "HMP60 and HMP110 Series User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M211060EN-N",
    "revision_date": "2025-02",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M211060EN-N/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 126-134"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats and 32-bit integers put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide's data-encoding section covers both formats and its worked read example confirms the order.",
    "A 16-bit integer reading of 0x8000 (32768) means the value is not available.",
    "Temperature-only models (HMP63T, HMP110T, HMP115T, TMP115) provide only temperature.",
    "Bit rate and parity changes (1538, 1539) take effect only after a restart (register 1542). Incompatible settings can lock you out of Modbus; Insight PC software can override them.",
    "Register 513 reads 0 when an error is active and 1 when there is none, as printed in the guide.",
    "Integer registers carry one decimal (raw x 0.1)."
  ],
